4	// Root cause this script exists for (issue #191):
5	// `actions/setup-node` with `registry-url` unconditionally writes
6	// `//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${N…KEN}` into the npm user
7	// config and exports the placeholder `XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX` when no token
8	// was supplied. npm then believes credentials are already configured, never
9	// performs the OIDC token exchange, and the registry rejects the anonymous
10	// PUT with a misleading `E404 Not Found - PUT .../meta-language`.
11	// See https://github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1551.
12	//
13	// Removing the placeholder line makes npm fall through to the trusted
14	// publishing (OIDC) path. When a real NPM_TOKEN is supplied the line is kept
15	// so the classic token flow still works as a bootstrap fallback.
